      title: 'Bring remote writes into a local view',
      lede: 'Handle shared memory values separately from local Runtime notifications, using sync from messages or a watch loop.',
      document: {
        sections: [
          {
            id: 'sync-stock',
            heading: 'Write stock from another Runtime',
            blocks: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Run sync-stock.ts with Node 24. Two Runtimes in one thread create separate views over one buffer; after writer changes it, stock.sync() notifies the local Effect.'
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Save as sync-stock.ts.'
              },
              {
                type: 'code',
                language: 'ts',
                code: "import { createRuntime } from '@migaia/reactive'\nimport { sharedInt32 } from '@migaia/store-shared'\nconst runtime = createRuntime()\nconst stock = sharedInt32(runtime, 2)\nconst writer = sharedInt32(createRuntime(), 0, stock.buffer)\nconst view = runtime.effect(() => console.log('Stock', stock.value))\ntry {\n  writer.value = 7\n  stock.sync()\n  runtime.flush()\n} finally {\n  view.dispose()\n  writer.dispose()\n  stock.dispose()\n}"
              },
              {
                type: 'code',
                language: 'text',
                code: 'Stock 2\nStock 7'
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            id: 'signal-members',
            heading: 'All public Signal members',
            blocks: [
              {
                type: 'table',
                headers: ['API, parameter, or field', 'Purpose, default, and return'],
                rows: [
                  [
                    'runtime / buffer',
                    'Readonly IRuntime and SharedArrayBuffer identifying local ownership and shared storage.'
                  ],
                  [
                    'disposed',
                    'A boolean set to true after dispose, without implying that shared storage was cleared.'
                  ],
                  [
                    'version',
                    'A number representing the local Runtime reactive version, separate from the shared bigint write sequence.'
                  ],
                  [
                    'value',
                    'Reads number by synchronizing, tracking this node, and reading consistently. Writes require int32; equal values do not advance shared versions or notify.'
                  ],
                  [
                    'peek()',
                    'Returns number by consistently reading current shared memory, without tracking, updating the local observed version, or notifying observers.'
                  ],
                  [
                    'sync()',
                    'Returns boolean, updating the local cursor and notifying when the shared version differs, or false when unchanged. It compares versions rather than values alone.'
                  ],
                  [
                    'watch(scheduler?: IScheduler)',
                    'Return a stop function for the waitAsync loop. The first watch captures its scheduler, default systemScheduler; active calls reuse both. Stopping or disposing ends the loop.'
                  ],
                  [
                    'dispose()',
                    'Returns void and repeated calls do not release it again. Stops watch and disconnects the local node. Later value, peek, sync, and watch access throws SIGNAL_DISPOSED.'
                  ],
                  [
                    'subs',
                    'ReadonlySet<IObserver> for graph inspection; applications do not add or remove subscriptions through it.'
                  ],
                  [
                    'onObserved() / onUnobserved()',
                    'Take no arguments, return void, and currently do nothing when called by reactive lifecycle handling.'
                  ],
                  [
                    'isStale()',
                    'Returns boolean by comparing shared and locally observed versions without notification; the current implementation has no disposed-state check.'
                  ]
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            id: 'read-notify',
            heading: 'Reading a value and notifying a view are separate',
            blocks: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'peek can read a new shared value without publishing local notifications. value synchronizes and tracks dependencies, but an existing Effect cannot discover remote writes by itself; use sync from a message callback or enable watch.'
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'sync can combine several remote writes into one local observation, so it is not a log of every operation. Applications needing each operation should send business messages; this package stores current integer state.'
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            id: 'backoff',
            heading: 'Contention handling belongs to the underlying reads and writes',
            blocks: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Current consistent reads and lock acquisition retry in rounds with backoff, reporting CONTENTION_LIMIT after sustained contention reaches a time bound. One spin-round limit is not the total attempt count. This page performs no contention or recovery measurement; see the seqlock page.'
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      next: [
        {
          path: 'shared-array-and-reactive-cells',
          label: 'Use shared arrays'
        },
        {
          path: 'seqlock-and-contention',
          label: 'Understand consistent reads and contention'
        }
      ]
