    en: {
      title: 'Let a price view read its selected entry',
      lede: 'Choose per-key or aggregate reads in an Effect and let the collection remove unobserved internal cell records.',
      document: {
        sections: [
          {
            id: 'tea-price',
            heading: 'Display the current tea price',
            blocks: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'The price-view.ts view reads tea only. Updating coffee leaves this output unchanged; updating tea produces the next displayed tea price.'
              },
              {
                type: 'code',
                language: 'ts',
                code: "import { createRuntime } from '@migaia/reactive'\nimport { ObservableMap } from '@migaia/store-indexed'\n\nconst runtime = createRuntime()\nconst prices = new ObservableMap([['tea', 10], ['coffee', 20]], runtime)\nconst view = runtime.effect(() => {\n  console.log('Tea price:', prices.get('tea'))\n})\ntry {\n  prices.set('coffee', 25)\n  prices.set('tea', 12)\n  runtime.flush()\n} finally {\n  view.dispose()\n  prices.dispose()\n}"
              },
              {
                type: 'code',
                language: 'text',
                code: 'Tea price: 10\nTea price: 12'
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            id: 'tracked-reads',
            heading: 'Record dependencies at the chosen read granularity',
            blocks: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'A cell is an internal Signal for a key, index, or member. Only tracked per-entry reads need one; calling get, at, or has outside tracking does not create a per-entry cell.'
              },
              {
                type: 'table',
                headers: ['Member or parameter', 'Purpose and return value'],
                rows: [
                  [
                    '`Object.get / Map.get`',
                    'Use value cells for tracked keys, including missing keys. Ordinary synchronous reads query storage directly.'
                  ],
                  [
                    '`Array.at`',
                    'Tracks the value at a valid index. Negative/out-of-range reads also observe length to detect position changes.'
                  ],
                  [
                    '`Object.has / Object.keys / Map.keys`',
                    'Track the entire key set without individual value cells. Object.has therefore differs from Map.has.'
                  ],
                  [
                    '`Map.has / Set.has`',
                    'Track a key value cell and a boolean membership cell respectively. Map.has can rerun when its key value changes.'
                  ],
                  [
                    '`Array.length / Map.size / Set.size`',
                    'Track overall length/membership structure, not the number of materialized cells.'
                  ],
                  [
                    '`Object.snapshot / Array.snapshot`',
                    'Track value revisions without individual entry cells and reuse shallow-frozen snapshots while the revision stays unchanged.'
                  ],
                  [
                    '`Map.valuesArray / entries / snapshot`',
                    'Track all content changes; changing any key value can rerun these reads.'
                  ],
                  [
                    '`Set.valuesArray / snapshot`',
                    'Track the whole membership set rather than one member.'
                  ],
                  [
                    '`Object.peek / Map.peek / Array.peek`',
                    'Do not track dependencies or create per-key cells even inside an Effect. Set has no peek method.'
                  ]
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            id: 'snapshots',
            heading: 'Distinguish readonly typing from frozen copies',
            blocks: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Object/Array snapshots are shallow-frozen and reused by revision. Map/Set snapshots are fresh native copies; changing a copy does not call collection writes. keys arrays are unfrozen; valuesArray and Map entries arrays are frozen.'
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Copies retain member-object references without recursively cloning or freezing them. Submit new values through collection methods to notify views rather than mutating nested snapshot objects.'
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            id: 'cell-lifetime',
            heading: 'End observation and reclaim cell records',
            blocks: [
              {
                type: 'table',
                headers: ['Member or parameter', 'Purpose and return value'],
                rows: [
                  [
                    'Start tracking',
                    'The first tracked get, at, or relevant has creates a cell; construction separately creates collection-level structure/revision nodes.'
                  ],
                  [
                    'Last observer leaves',
                    'onUnobserved tries to remove it from the cell table and collection bookkeeping while business data remains stored.'
                  ],
                  [
                    'No observer remains',
                    'Creation schedules a check through the owning Runtime idle channel and removes the current unobserved record. Microtasks are the default; scheduleIdle can supply the host channel.'
                  ],
                  [
                    'Deleted while observed',
                    'Keeps the cell with missing/false state so observers see deletion; removing observers allows record reclamation.'
                  ],
                  [
                    '`prune()`',
                    'Object/Map/Set can retire records of deleted entries; arrays expose no such method. Retirement neither cancels observers nor measures host GC.'
                  ],
                  [
                    '`dispose(): void`',
                    'Disposes reactive nodes still registered by the collection; later reads/writes fail. The collection does not automatically call dispose when unused.'
                  ]
                ]
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Automatic reclamation here removes cell records and bookkeeping; it does not delete business data or prove immediate host memory collection. This page executes the normal price view and describes microtask cleanup from source.'
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            id: 'runtime-and-cleanup',
            heading: 'Use one Runtime for the collection and its observer',
            blocks: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Tracking from another Runtime fails. Per-key checks may produce this package CROSS_RUNTIME, while direct structural Signal reads may produce the same code from reactive; inspect the actual source/code pair.'
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Dispose the observing Effect before the collection. See [disposal and errors](/en/docs/store-indexed/disposal-and-errors) for error classification and full cleanup; this page does not add failure scenarios.'
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      next: [
        {
          label: 'Bulk replacement and pruning',
          path: 'bulk-replacement-and-pruning'
        },
        {
          label: 'Mutation guards and Runtime',
          path: 'mutation-guards-and-runtime'
        }
      ]
    }
