            heading: 'Use returned memory and named conversion functions',
            blocks: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: '`InitOutput.memory` supplies linear memory. Import `json_to_msgpack()` and `msgpack_to_json()` by name for application conversion. The same names on the initialization object are raw WASM functions returning a numeric object address, rather than `ConversionResult`.'
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'The table lists every public `InitOutput` member. Application code usually reads only `memory`; generated JavaScript wrappers use the others. A raw result object address is not an arena allocation ID.'
              },
              {
                type: 'table',
                headers: ['Initialization result member', 'Description'],
                rows: [
                  [
                    '`memory`',
                    'This `WebAssembly.Memory` exposes the current `memory.buffer`. Allocation may invalidate an earlier byte view.'
                  ],
                  [
                    '`alloc_bytes(a)`',
                    '`a` is the requested byte count; the result is a numeric allocation ID. Applications use the named function described on the memory page.'
                  ],
                  [
                    '`byte_len_of(a)`',
                    '`a` is an allocation ID. The returned numeric capacity can exceed the exact conversion length.'
                  ],
                  ['`ptr_of(a)`', 'Returns a numeric byte offset for wrappers and memory views.'],
                  [
                    '`dealloc_bytes(a)`',
                    'Returns numeric `0` or `1`. The named export converts this to a boolean.'
                  ],
                  [
                    '`json_to_msgpack(a, b)`',
                    'Pass input ID and read length. The result object address is wrapped as `ConversionResult` by the named export.'
                  ],
                  [
                    '`msgpack_to_json(a, b)`',
                    'Input ID and byte length select the bytes to read. It returns a result object address, which applications cannot treat as an output ID.'
                  ],
                  [
                    '`conversionresult_id(a)`',
                    '`a` is a result object address. It returns the numeric output allocation ID used by the wrapper `id` getter.'
                  ],
                  [
                    '`conversionresult_len(a)`',
                    'The result object address produces a numeric output byte count for the wrapper `len` getter.'
                  ],
                  [
                    '`conversionresult_error(a)`',
                    'The result object address produces `[number, number]`: temporary error text byte offset and length.'
                  ],
                  [
                    '`__wbg_conversionresult_free(a, b)`',
                    '`a` is the object address and `b` is a release flag: `0` for manual release or `1` in the finalizer. It returns `void`; applications call wrapper `free()`.'
                  ],
                  [
                    '`__wbindgen_externrefs`',
                    'This `WebAssembly.Table` stores JavaScript references needed by generated code, rather than application byte data.'
                  ],
                  [
                    '`__wbindgen_free(a, b, c)`',
                    'The arguments are address, length, and alignment. It returns `void`, releasing temporary error strings for generated code.'
                  ],
                  [
                    '`__wbindgen_start()`',
                    'It takes no arguments and returns `void`. Initialization invokes it automatically to prepare the generated runtime.'
                  ]
                ]
              }
            ]
