    en: {
      title: 'Add a report plugin while running',
      lede: 'A managed Host keeps definitions separate from ready plugins. Mutate the managed object and read its published view while Tray coordinates the underlying PluginHost creation, installation, and closure.',
      document: {
        sections: [
          {
            id: 'add-report',
            heading: 'Enable report rendering',
            blocks: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'managed-host.ts constructs a real PluginHost, report-plugin.ts supplies report rendering, and dynamic.ts installs it in an empty Host. These files form one scene; other dynamic topics reuse the same support files.'
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'managed-host.ts'
              },
              {
                type: 'code',
                language: 'ts',
                code: "import { PluginHost } from '@migaia/plugin-host'\nimport { createHost, type ICreateHostOptions, type ITrayPluginConstraint } from '@migaia/tray/host'\nexport class AppHost extends PluginHost<Record<string, never>, string> {}\nexport const openHost = <const T extends readonly ITrayPluginConstraint<AppHost>[]>(\n  plugins: T & ICreateHostOptions<AppHost, T>['plugins']\n) =>\n  createHost<AppHost, T>({\n    create: () => new AppHost({\n      execution: { mutationTimeoutMs: false, pipelineDrainTimeoutMs: false }\n    }),\n    plugins,\n    mutationAdmissionMs: 100,\n    quiescenceMs: 0,\n    shutdown: { mode: 'bounded' }\n  })"
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'report-plugin.ts'
              },
              {
                type: 'code',
                language: 'ts',
                code: "export const report = {\n  name: 'report',\n  install: () => ({ render: () => 'October report' })\n} as const\nexport const reportPlugins = [report] as const"
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'dynamic.ts'
              },
              {
                type: 'code',
                language: 'ts',
                code: "import { openHost } from './managed-host.ts'\nimport { report } from './report-plugin.ts'\nconst host = await openHost([])\ntry {\n  const result = await host.use(report)\n  if (result.ok) console.log(result.view.extensions.render())\n  console.log(JSON.stringify(host.readyPlugins))\n} finally {\n  const closed = await host.dispose()\n  await closed.physicalCompletion\n}"
              },
              {
                type: 'code',
                language: 'text',
                code: 'October report\n["report"]'
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'A successful result.view carries the added plugin’s extension type. The original host remains the same running object, but its existing TypeScript type does not change after use; use the successful view for new extensions.'
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            id: 'creation-options',
            heading: 'Choose waiting policies at creation',
            blocks: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: '[createHost](/en/docs/tray/api/host/createHost) accepts [ICreateHostOptions](/en/docs/tray/api/host/ICreateHostOptions) and returns a managed Host after its initial graph starts. Its factory must return a fresh PluginHost not already claimed by another manager.'
              },
              {
                type: 'table',
                headers: ['Member / setting', 'Purpose and default behavior'],
                rows: [
                  [
                    'create',
                    'Required synchronous factory for the sole underlying PluginHost, which Tray eventually closes. Do not mutate its plugins outside the managed object.'
                  ],
                  [
                    'plugins',
                    'Required initial definition array; empty is valid. Constructor-installed baseline plugins remain in views. Feature, config, and release entries are captured once.'
                  ],
                  [
                    '`mutationAdmissionMs`',
                    'Required finite nonnegative waiting-to-start budget for serialized graph operations, rather than task execution duration. The example uses 100.'
                  ],
                  [
                    'quiescenceMs',
                    'Required finite nonnegative physical-cleanup waiting budget in bounded mode. The example uses 0 and retains the returned cleanup Promise.'
                  ],
                  [
                    'shutdown.mode',
                    'Required: bounded may return before cleanup finishes; strict-drain waits for actual cleanup. Neither forcibly terminates a running Promise.'
                  ],
                  [
                    'report(error)?',
                    'No caller reporter by default; a supplied callback receives lifecycle/cleanup diagnostics. Reporter failure is contained without replacing the operation result.'
                  ]
                ]
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Host `execution.pipelineDrainTimeoutMs` remains required. A number gives one shared cleanup budget across pipeline steps and leases, rather than restarting it per item. `false` waits for actual completion. After an early return, observe later cleanup through the result’s `physicalCompletion`.'
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'The Graph binding fence still finishes first. The numeric pipeline budget does not bypass that fence or cancel a running Promise.'
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            id: 'managed-view',
            heading: 'Read and observe the managed object',
            blocks: [
              {
                type: 'table',
                headers: ['Member / setting', 'Purpose and default behavior'],
                rows: [
                  [
                    'plugins / readyPlugins',
                    'List admitted definitions and ready plugin names respectively. A definition missing a required provider remains in plugins but not readyPlugins.'
                  ],
                  [
                    'extensions / config',
                    'Expose baseline and ready-plugin extension/config views, excluding blocked functionality. There is no additional public getShared method.'
                  ],
                  [
                    'pluginState(name)',
                    'Read a definition’s graph state, including blocked versus ready; an unknown name does not establish successful installation.'
                  ],
                  [
                    'state / isActive / error',
                    'state is active/closing/terminal/failed; isActive reports operation availability and error retains Host failure. terminal alone does not prove physical release.'
                  ],
                  [
                    'use(plugin) / replace(plugin) / unUse(name)',
                    'Add, replace the same name, or remove through the same serialized manager. The next page details results. Avoid bypassing it to mutate the underlying Host.'
                  ],
                  [
                    'dispose() / [Symbol.asyncDispose]()',
                    'dispose reuses its closure Promise and returns cleanup details. Symbol.asyncDispose waits on that closure and returns void; see physical cleanup for remaining work.'
                  ],
                  [
                    'on(type, listener)',
                    'Listeners receive an event context with event.value and a synchronous unsubscribe receipt. Sync/async listener failures are reported without rolling back committed changes.'
                  ]
                ]
              },
              {
                type: 'table',
                headers: ['Member / setting', 'Purpose and default behavior'],
                rows: [
                  [
                    'use / unUse / replace',
                    'Publish object payloads after operations settle. registered/removed/replaced are lifecycle aliases, not another mutation path.'
                  ],
                  [
                    'mutationFailed',
                    'Carries operation/name/error. Inspect committed on the actual result before deciding whether the definition remains current.'
                  ],
                  [
                    'disposing / disposed',
                    'Carry state:closing and state:terminal plus cleanupComplete respectively. Events do not replace awaiting physicalCompletion.'
                  ]
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            id: 'types',
            heading: 'Retain known extension types',
            blocks: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: '[ITrayResolvedHost](/en/docs/tray/api/host/ITrayResolvedHost) infers the ready set for finite literal tuples and provider names within 128 definitions. Widened names/arrays, erased provider information, or a larger set use [ITrayHostDynamic](/en/docs/tray/api/host/ITrayHostDynamic).'
              },
              {
                type: 'table',
                headers: ['Member / setting', 'Purpose and default behavior'],
                rows: [
                  [
                    'ICanResolveReadyDefinitions / IResolveReadyTrayPlugins',
                    'Determine whether exact inference is safe and compute ready definitions at compile time without starting plugins.'
                  ],
                  [
                    'IHostBaselinePlugins / ITrayPluginConstraint',
                    'Retain constructor baseline types and the PluginHost constraint. Dynamic views keep baseline extensions while unknown managed keys remain unknown.'
                  ],
                  [
                    'IPluginWithSynchronousShared',
                    'Constrains a declared shared result to a synchronous object; asynchronous shared work cannot establish an already published synchronous view.'
                  ]
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      next: [
        {
          label: 'Handle dependencies and mutation results',
          path: 'mutation-and-blocking'
        }
      ]
    }
