                text: 'Built-in codec objects are frozen with `Object.freeze()`. `ICodec<TValue, TEncoded, TId = string, TVersion = number>` describes the five members above and requires no `dispose()`. Registry parsers accept context and return chunks, so the two objects are not directly interchangeable.'
